    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="0360" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg348"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890G.24/35: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Farrell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-30T23:00:00-04:00">June 30, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>126. Your 127, June 22, 1 p.m. With further reference to your 127, June 22, 1
                    p.m., the War Department states that the operations of Douglas in Iran are
                    carried out under contract with that Department. The operations of Pan American
                    are also performed under War Department contract. It is added that General
                        Fitzgerald<anchor n="11" xml:id="d408-f1"/> will proceed to Cairo in order
                    to command ferry operations in Africa and the Middle East and that the
                    operations of Pan American in those areas will be under his supervision and
                    direct control.</p>
                <p>In view of the nature of the activities of the War Department and contract
                    organizations in Iraq and neighboring areas, the Department assumes that a
                    satisfactory arrangement with the Iraqi authorities will be obtained promptly
                    and without difficulty.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d408-f1" n="11" xml:id="d408-f1-content">
                <p>Brig. Gen. S. W. Fitzgerald, Commanding General, U. S. Army Forces in Central
                    Africa.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
